Shared helpers for the eng-* cases (no cmd file, so cases.sh skips this
directory). Cases use them as "$CASE/../eng-lib/<file>".

csv.awk   checks a CircuitCSV output file and prints selected columns rounded.
          -v show="Col:decimals,Col,..."  columns to print (no decimals = as is)
          -v mono=Col                     Col must not decrease down the file
          Prints BAD lines for NaN/inf, the 99.9 sentinel, magnitudes over 1e6
          and unknown Status values; cases reject "BAD".
prop.awk  checks the "Calculated Parameters" block of an ITURHFProp report:
          BAD for NaN/inf or the 99.9 sentinel, then prints the requested
          1-based columns rounded: -v show="4:0,16,..."
          It also prints BAD when the dominant mode's loss (column 52) is
          below free space over twice its reflection height (column 54),
          which the slant range of eq. (19) can never be. That needs the
          RPT_ALLMODES column layout that path.tmpl selects.
path.tmpl an ITURHFProp input with @...@ placeholders filled in by sed.
